# Radiology and Imaging Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct Radiology flow source of truth for HOSSPI HMS. Radiology is an **executing department** — every order links to a **clinical encounter** (`encounter_id`). Radiology does not create OPD/IPD encounters or advance patient flow stages directly. Align with [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable radiology staff to execute order-to-report workflows: receive orders, schedule and perform studies, manage imaging assets, draft and finalize reports, sync to PACS where configured, and release results to clinicians.

### Central encounter rule

Orders attach to OPD or IPD encounters. Radiology executes studies and reports; Clinical places orders; OPD/IPD orchestrators own stage progression.

---

## 2. Position in the Patient Journey

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    OPD[OPD RADIOLOGY_REQUESTED] --> RAD[Radiology workbench]
    IPD[IPD order — ipd-flow §7] --> RAD
    CLIN[Clinical order dialog] --> RAD
    RAD --> REPORT[Report finalized]
    REPORT --> OPD_DONE[OPD stage updated by orchestrator]
    REPORT --> IPD_TL[IPD timeline / care loop §8]
```

| Source | Flow reference | Radiology responsibility |
| ------ | -------------- | ------------------------ |
| OPD | [opd-flow §3](./opd-flow.mdc) `RADIOLOGY_REQUESTED`, `LAB_AND_RADIOLOGY_REQUESTED` | Workbench shows OPD orders |
| IPD | [ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc) imaging route | Scan → report on admission encounter |
| Billing | [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc) | `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel` at order |
| Biomedical | [app-write-up](../app-write-up.mdc) | Equipment **maintenance** is Biomedical — radiology consumes equipment for scheduling only |

---

## 3. Step-by-Step Radiology Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Order received | Order on radiology workbench. | System |
| 2 | Billing gate (if required) | Pay-now or bill-later. | Cashier / System |
| 3 | Scheduling / assignment | Assign modality, room, equipment. | Radiology clerk |
| 4 | Study start | Patient scanned; study record created. | Radiographer |
| 5 | Asset capture | Images uploaded; PACS sync if configured. | Radiographer / System |
| 6 | Report draft | Radiologist drafts report. | Radiologist |
| 7 | Finalization / attestation | Final report released. | Radiologist |
| 8 | Addendum (if needed) | Corrected or supplemental report. | Radiologist |

---

## 4. Backend Workbench Contract

Use `/api/v1/radiology/*` workspace routes as canonical. Order pipeline: assign → start → complete → cancel; study workflow with asset upload and PACS; result draft → finalize → attestation → addendum.

---

## 5. Role and Module Boundaries

| Rule | Detail |
| ---- | ------ |
| [opd-flow §5](./opd-flow.mdc) | Radiology workspace only — no OPD stage mutations from radiology UI |
| Clinical boundary | Orders via `clinical_radiology_order_action_dialog.dart` |
| Biomedical boundary | Imaging equipment registry/PM is not radiology workflow ownership |

